      "id": "bug-013",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-09T17:40:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "AP build: duplicate case values in autopilot_static.c (AP_MODE_RATE_DIRECT==3 clashes with AP_MODE_KILL==3 from generated header)",
      "file": "paparazzi/var/aircrafts/ANTON_MFC/Makefile.ac",
      "root_cause": "Makefile.ac generation caches by mtime: generator only overwrites Makefile.ac if it is older than source XMLs. After an NPS build, Makefile.ac has USE_GENERATED_AUTOPILOT=TRUE only in the NPS block. AP build reuses this stale file, so autopilot_static.c is compiled alongside the generated autopilot header, causing duplicate case value errors.",
      "fix": "build_fw.sh now always deletes var/aircrafts/<AC>/Makefile.ac before each build, forcing the generator to regenerate it for the current target. This ensures USE_GENERATED_AUTOPILOT=TRUE appears in the correct target block regardless of which target was built last.",
      "tags": [
        "build",
        "makefile",
        "autopilot",
        "generated-autopilot",
        "caching"
      ],
      "related_bugs": [],
      "occurrences": 2,
