    {
      "id": "bug-020",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-10T12:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "pprz_version.h:58 error: invalid type argument of unary '*' (have 'int') in PPRZ_VERSION_INT, when compiling autopilot.c during `build_active.sh ... fast`. Intermittent: only when autopilot.o is actually recompiled.",
      "file": "build_active.sh",
      "root_cause": "The fast path runs `make -C paparazzi/sw/airborne all` directly, bypassing Makefile.ac which computes/exports GIT_DESC, PPRZ_VER, PPRZ_VER_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH. sw/airborne/Makefile:59-64 then emits -DPPRZ_VER_MAJOR= (empty) into CFLAGS, so PPRZ_VERSION_INT expands to ( * 10000 + * 100 + ). Only autopilot.c expands that macro, so the error is latent until an edit forces autopilot.o to rebuild ('when more files are affected').",
      "fix": "build_active.sh fast block now recreates the version vars (mirroring Makefile.ac, including the PPRZ_VER_PATCH=0 guard since v7.0_unstable has no patch field) and passes GIT_SHA1/GIT_DESC/PPRZ_VER/PPRZ_VER_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH on the make command line.",
      "tags": [
        "build",
        "makefile",
        "fast-build",
        "pprz_version",
        "autopilot",
        "version-macro"
      ],
      "related_bugs": [
        "bug-013"
      ],
      "occurrences": 1,
      "last_seen": "2026-06-10T12:00:00.000Z"
